  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ending Neglected Diseases through Operational Research (ENDOR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Global Health (GH)):  Funds will support the optimization of NTD control and elimination, coordinated by the Task Force for Global Health, through the following: define and research operational roadblocks that hinder the successful implementation of NTD programs and progress toward control and elimination goals; link and engage researchers, country-level program staff, implementation partners, and the donor community to build and accelerate consensus to answer key operational questions; support operational research to improve mapping strategies; develop tools and strategies to improve mass drug administration coverage and close compliance gaps; reduce existing morbidity; optimize and develop new diagnostics; and build capacity by awarding small grants to young African researchers working in NTDs. These activities aim to remove barriers and improve program efficiencies to safeguard NTD investments...ENDOR supports a research agenda on the nascent field of female genital schistosomiasis with an emphasis on diagnosis, healthcare worker clinical competencies, and linkage to the health system.</narrative>
  </description>
